# The seven source files of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_ifa.py reads them from sources/nist/ (git-ignored). The Validators
# workflow downloads them from the base below, checks them against this list
# with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter and fails if the conversion in this
# folder comes out different. The bundle, the two coverage reports and the
# ledger are therefore a reproducible record: a change of the kernel, of
# oscal_conv_lib.py or of the converter that would alter them is noticed.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/usnistgov/oscal-content/9402f031/
# path: examples/component-definition/json/example-component-definition.json
# path: examples/ap/json/ifa_assessment-plan.json
# path: examples/ar/json/ifa_assessment-results.json
# path: examples/poam/json/ifa_plan-of-action-and-milestones.json
# path: examples/ssp/json/ifa_ssp.json
# path: examples/ssp/json/oscal_leveraged-example_ssp.json
# path: examples/ssp/json/oscal_leveraging-example_ssp.json
#
